            <div class="col s12 m8 paragraphStyleNews">
                <p>
                    Blue Shades, Vilpa Max’s original animated series, is officially in production. Set in a dystopian
                    world where Artificial Intelligence dictates creativity, this sci-fi thriller is custom-built for
                    fans seeking a narrative that hits dangerously close to our current reality.
                </p>
                <p>
                    But how did Blue Shades come to be in the first place, and who are the people behind it all?
                </p>
                <h5 class="bolderFont" style="color: rgb(75, 75, 75) !important;">
                    A Call for Independent Thinkers
                </h5>
                <p>
                    The series was born from the imagination of Vilpa Max’s founder, Alejandro Vilpa, who has had past
                    experience with his two novels on the mafia (The Afterlife of Rebecca Smirnov) and mystery (The
                    Breath of the Innocents) respectively. Vilpa names Denisse Nilo Segovia as a key mentor in his
                    initial work drafting Blue Shades, as mentioned in an interview with the Tokyo International Film
                    Festival.
                </p>
                <p>
                    “Blue Shades is a world I created to reflect the struggles artists face in a society where
                    creativity is controlled and individuality is discouraged,” Vilpa shared in response to a query on
                    his inspiration for the series.
                </p>
                <p>
                    “It is a call to action for people - artists and non-artists alike - to think for themselves, feel
                    for themselves, and question the systems that shape their reality.”
                </p>
                <p>
                    When asked about what he hopes for the series, Vilpa said, “Blue Shades is not just the beginning of
                    a series; it is an artistic movement intended to inspire a new generation of independent thinkers.”
                </p>
                <h5 class="bolderFont" style="color: rgb(75, 75, 75) !important;">
                    The Voices of the Resistance
                </h5>
                <p>
                    Blue Shades stars Carla Aguilar López as Elisa, an outlawed artist who is trying to investigate her
                    brother’s disappearance in a world where AI has completely overtaken human creativity. Lopez is most
                    known for her role as Ivana in the film short ‘The Undertone of David Jansen’, which Vilpa also
                    wrote and directed.
                </p>
                <img class="responsive-img" src="/assets/images/carlita.jpg" style="border-radius: 25px ;">
                <p class="dateAesteticTitle2 center">Actress Carla Aguilar López</p>
                <p>
                    She is joined by her co-star, Dimitri Fontaine, who plays Hassan - Elisa’s longtime friend and
                    collaborator, assisting her in collecting industry secrets from the biggest AI companies in Blue
                    District, where the story is set. For Fontaine’s, this role will mark his debut as an actor.
                </p>
                <img class="responsive-img" src="/assets/images/dimitrito.jpg" style="border-radius: 25px ;">
                <p class="dateAesteticTitle2 center">Actor Dimitri Fontaine</p>
                <h5 class="bolderFont" style="color: rgb(75, 75, 75) !important;">
                    Premium Production in Motion
                </h5>
                <p>
                    To bring this ambitious cyberpunk aesthetic to life, the project is overseen by Head of Production
                    Ivan Surnyk, known for his extensive work across TV series and music videos. The visual identity is
                    spearheaded by Lead Animator Arseniy Oleinik (director of the animated short Café).
                </p>
                <p>
                    Complementing the striking visuals, the sonic identity of the series is being crafted by artist
                    Federico Casazza. He is working in close collaboration with Dimitri Fontaine himself, who will
                    perform the series’ main theme—a powerful rap track that promises to become the definitive anthem of
                    the story's rebellion.
                </p>
                <p>
                    With animation tests for the cast recently wrapped, the production pipeline is officially in full
                    swing. Blue Shades is slated to make its grand premiere at the Dubai International Content Market
                    (DICM)—MENA’s largest gathering of media professionals—taking place November 10-11 at the Madinat
                    Jumeirah, where Alejandro Vilpa will also be featured as a panel speaker.
                </p>
                <h4 class="bolderFont" style="color: black !important;">
                    About Vilpa Max
                </h4>
                <p>
                    Vilpa Max is a curated streaming platform where award-winning cinema meets bold new voices—featuring
                    Oscar-winning, Oscar-nominated, BAFTA-winning, and Cannes-selected films from around the world. <br>
                    <br>
                    Watch on Vilpa Max: <br> <br>
                    <a href="https://vilpamax.com/" target="_blank">www.vilpamax.com</a> <br> <br>
                    Available in the UK and across the MENA region.
                </p>


